The function is already minimal, so there is little to gain. This version only reorders work slightly:

- It reads `type` into a local once.
- It marks the cached-`type` path as the likely branch with `__builtin_expect`, which helps the compiler lay out the common case as straight-line code.
- It loads `profile` into a local once.

Behavior is unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    if ((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```